“No, it’s not absurd. We just have to ﬁnd a way.” He lowered his head and put a hand on his forehead. “Maybe
. . . maybe if he invests his money in the wrong way . . . if he buys shares, paying far more than their value, as in the South Sea Bubble . . .” He cupped his hands together and blew into them to warm them up. “You understand, right?”
“Hmm?”
“No, you don’t understand.” He let out a sigh. “Chris, studying a bit more really wouldn’t hurt you.”
