Of course, the name. Christopher was silent, clenching his ﬁsts in the ice-cold air. Oh, Frank had been so ﬁrm when he had imposed that name “Davenport” on him! Wasn’t it now clear why? Martha had asked him for that years before, and in response at that time a no had killed her. A belated sense of guilt—that was his bloody name. And he could not get rid of it! He couldn’t, for God’s sake! Because Leopold DeMercy would never connect Christopher Davenport with

the obscure and forgotten Martha Askey from his past, since that name—that damned name, that hated name—was good for something, damn it!
